1
00:00:34,972 --> 00:00:36,140
[This drama is fictional
and bears no resemblance to reality]

2
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:37,142
[Some scenes feature AI technology]

3
00:00:37,142 --> 00:00:38,063
[All child and animal scenes
followed strict safety guidelines]

4
00:01:04,108 --> 00:01:06,167
What was that just now?

5
00:01:08,056 --> 00:01:10,185
That's what I should be asking.

6
00:01:12,711 --> 00:01:14,783
What on earth was I thinking?

7
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:16,879
Jeez.

8
00:01:16,879 --> 00:01:19,746
- What's wrong with you, Ju Yi Jae?
- Forget it. Don't follow me!

9
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:21,406
Hey, Ju Yi Jae! You're getting soaked!

10
00:01:21,406 --> 00:01:24,747
Fine! I won't follow you,
so at least take the umbrella!

11
00:01:24,747 --> 00:01:26,967
- Forget it.
- Huh?

12
00:01:26,967 --> 00:01:28,890
You'll catch a cold!

13
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:31,839
It's none of your business if I do!

14
00:01:33,709 --> 00:01:35,769
[Episode 5]

15
00:01:42,041 --> 00:01:43,942
Oh, you're back?

16
00:01:43,942 --> 00:01:46,810
"Oh... you're back?"

17
00:01:46,810 --> 00:01:50,146
Oh, sorry. Just pretend it never happened.

18
00:01:50,146 --> 00:01:52,239
How do you pretend something that happened
never happened?

19
00:01:52,239 --> 00:01:55,469
I guess writing that kissing scene
messed with my head.

20
00:01:55,469 --> 00:01:57,367
You didn't even write it.

21
00:01:57,367 --> 00:02:00,222
I guess I lost it
just thinking about writing it.

22
00:02:01,205 --> 00:02:03,100
Maybe it's for the best.

23
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:06,566
We needed to get this
out of the way eventually.

24
00:02:06,566 --> 00:02:08,019
Get what out of the way?

25
00:02:08,019 --> 00:02:11,146
I needed to figure out how I really felt.

26
00:02:11,146 --> 00:02:12,856
We're working together now,

27
00:02:12,856 --> 00:02:15,527
and we can't let personal feelings
get in the way.

28
00:02:15,527 --> 00:02:17,293
So?

29
00:02:17,293 --> 00:02:19,431
Did you get your answer?

30
00:02:19,431 --> 00:02:21,620
The kiss belonged in the script...

31
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:23,651
but we shouldn't have done it.

32
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:28,261
Look at me when you say that.

33
00:02:28,261 --> 00:02:30,855
Look at what?

34
00:02:30,855 --> 00:02:32,307
Look at me.

35
00:02:33,115 --> 00:02:36,365
We spent so much time together,
I got confused, okay?

36
00:02:36,365 --> 00:02:37,446
You were always right there,

37
00:02:37,446 --> 00:02:41,177
so my eyes kept going to you,
and I couldn't stop thinking about you...

38
00:02:41,177 --> 00:02:43,738
I... I'll make sure it never happens again.

39
00:02:43,738 --> 00:02:46,017
I'm sorry if I made you uncomfortable.

40
00:02:46,831 --> 00:02:50,546
If that's your answer,
then I don't want your apology.

41
00:02:50,546 --> 00:02:54,137
We don't have to lay our feelings
completely bare to each other.

42
00:02:54,137 --> 00:02:56,220
So from now on, deal with your own feelings.

43
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:58,974
Don't use me to figure them out.

44
00:02:58,974 --> 00:03:02,075
Acting like this is so childish.

45
00:03:02,075 --> 00:03:04,716
We're not 18 anymore.

46
00:03:11,376 --> 00:03:14,172
Okay! I'll do it the American way too.

47
00:03:14,172 --> 00:03:15,966
<i>The kiss belonged in the script...</i>

48
00:03:15,966 --> 00:03:17,573
<i>but we shouldn't have done it.</i>

49
00:03:17,573 --> 00:03:19,368
Just move on?

50
00:03:20,826 --> 00:03:21,845
Then why did you kiss me?

51
00:03:21,845 --> 00:03:24,299
<i>We spent so much time together, I got confused.</i>

52
00:03:24,299 --> 00:03:26,205
Did I get played?

53
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:34,447
- Ju Yi Jae!
- What?

54
00:03:34,447 --> 00:03:36,108
Go home.

55
00:03:41,147 --> 00:03:43,473
You think I won't leave
just because you told me to?

56
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:45,686
You're unbelievable.

57
00:03:45,686 --> 00:03:49,396
Who's the childish one now? Darn it...

58
00:03:49,396 --> 00:03:53,105
Fine. Whatever. I'm leaving.

59
00:03:58,811 --> 00:04:01,409
Hey! I was leaving anyway!

60
00:04:01,409 --> 00:04:04,311
I'm leaving because I choose to!

61
00:04:38,595 --> 00:04:39,988
What?

62
00:04:39,988 --> 00:04:42,617
Soo Bin asked me to come get you.

63
00:04:42,617 --> 00:04:44,336
He said it's not safe to walk alone this late.

64
00:04:44,336 --> 00:04:46,923
Seriously? That's ridiculous.

65
00:04:46,923 --> 00:04:50,832
I know. He worries about everything.

66
00:04:51,976 --> 00:04:54,002
I'll protect you.

67
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:55,712
Have you lost your mind?

68
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:58,875
So what now?

69
00:04:58,875 --> 00:05:00,365
What do you mean?

70
00:05:00,365 --> 00:05:02,724
You're done running away
and coming home, aren't you?

71
00:05:03,929 --> 00:05:05,884
- Oh...
- "Oh?"

72
00:05:05,884 --> 00:05:09,110
- Then why'd you come here?
- Where's Mom?

73
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:10,782
She's at the restaurant.

74
00:05:12,314 --> 00:05:13,641
Just go home first.

75
00:05:13,641 --> 00:05:16,244
- Why?
- Just go home!

76
00:05:33,125 --> 00:05:34,785
<i>Hello!</i>

77
00:05:34,785 --> 00:05:37,649
<i>It's amazing she can balance that on her head.</i>

78
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:42,621
<i>- Wow, she's really good.
- Nothing's falling off.</i>

79
00:05:42,621 --> 00:05:46,217
<i>- Thank you!
- That's amazing!</i>

80
00:05:51,393 --> 00:05:54,520
<i>Ugh, it's slipping away! Catch it, catch it!</i>

81
00:06:12,021 --> 00:06:13,642
Mom.

82
00:06:15,934 --> 00:06:17,714
I'm hungry.

83
00:06:27,251 --> 00:06:28,891
I eat carrots now, you know.

84
00:06:28,891 --> 00:06:31,892
It's not like you suddenly started liking them.

85
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:34,348
Don't force yourself to eat something you hate.

86
00:06:34,348 --> 00:06:37,104
Seeing you climb mountains on that injured leg,

87
00:06:37,104 --> 00:06:39,592
fall into the sea even though
you're scared of water,

88
00:06:39,592 --> 00:06:42,522
and smile while eating food you hate...

89
00:06:43,298 --> 00:06:45,987
I hated seeing you like that.

90
00:06:46,615 --> 00:06:49,027
It hurt so much.

91
00:06:59,784 --> 00:07:01,588
From now on,
if you don't like something, say so.

92
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:03,837
Just do whatever you want every day.

93
00:07:03,837 --> 00:07:07,806
Just live thinking about what makes you
happy today and tomorrow...

94
00:07:10,055 --> 00:07:12,315
Just live like that from now on.

95
00:07:12,315 --> 00:07:16,619
Don't worry about Young Jae or me.

96
00:07:17,796 --> 00:07:19,879
- Mom...
- Don't talk.

97
00:07:19,879 --> 00:07:22,329
Noodles coming out of your mouth.

98
00:07:28,458 --> 00:07:31,086
Directors just work sitting down, right?

99
00:07:35,818 --> 00:07:38,101
Well, then that's fine.

100
00:07:42,254 --> 00:07:44,354
But, Yi Jae...

101
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:49,519
If you're going to work with him,

102
00:07:50,512 --> 00:07:53,659
you should tell him about it.

103
00:07:55,034 --> 00:07:57,019
I'm saying this for your own good.

104
00:07:57,019 --> 00:08:00,720
When people hide something,
it tends to show up in strange ways.

105
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,178
Grandma?

106
00:08:45,361 --> 00:08:46,760
Huh?

107
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:50,031
Grandma?

108
00:08:53,226 --> 00:08:56,552
Grandma, Grandma!

109
00:08:56,552 --> 00:08:58,580
Are you okay, Grandma?

110
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:01,499
Grandma? Grandma!

111
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:03,192
[Woo General Hospital]

112
00:09:03,192 --> 00:09:07,181
Thankfully, we treated her in time
and she's out of immediate danger.

113
00:09:07,181 --> 00:09:09,428
It was hypoglycemic shock.

114
00:09:09,428 --> 00:09:14,108
Given her age, I recommend she stay
in the hospital for a few days,

115
00:09:14,108 --> 00:09:16,387
so we can monitor her and run some tests.

116
00:09:16,387 --> 00:09:18,794
Yes, thank you, Doctor.

117
00:09:24,953 --> 00:09:26,833
Hey.

118
00:09:26,833 --> 00:09:28,947
Don't you recognize me?

119
00:09:31,325 --> 00:09:32,809
Huh?

120
00:09:33,559 --> 00:09:35,216
Lee Mi Hyun?

121
00:09:37,519 --> 00:09:41,164
<i>Nice, nice. Good expression!</i>

122
00:09:41,164 --> 00:09:42,828
Wow!

123
00:09:42,828 --> 00:09:46,247
You looked good on TV,
but you look even better in person.

124
00:09:46,247 --> 00:09:48,190
You look like a celebrity.

125
00:09:48,190 --> 00:09:51,449
Have you been doing well?
I never expected to run into you here.

126
00:09:51,449 --> 00:09:55,615
Well, as you can see, this is my life now.

127
00:09:55,615 --> 00:09:57,407
I heard you came back.

128
00:09:57,407 --> 00:10:00,365
I heard you ate at my Mother's restaurant
the other day.

129
00:10:00,365 --> 00:10:02,895
- Me?
- Didn't you go to "Jinsusungchan" with Yi Jae?

130
00:10:02,895 --> 00:10:05,163
Oh, isn't that Jin Su's mom's restaurant?

131
00:10:05,163 --> 00:10:07,890
Oh... oh!

132
00:10:07,890 --> 00:10:13,090
Well, Jin Su's mom is my mother-in-law.

133
00:10:14,039 --> 00:10:15,838
- Huh?
- Yeah.

134
00:10:17,151 --> 00:10:19,504
- So, you and Jin Su?
- Yeah.

135
00:10:19,504 --> 00:10:21,458
Ah... huh?

136
00:10:22,122 --> 00:10:26,191
<i>- Hey! Can't you pedal faster?
- Run faster, you little brat!</i>

137
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:30,019
<i>- Isn't this makeup a bit too much?
- Ready!</i>

138
00:10:32,508 --> 00:10:35,632
- Oh, so that's how things ended up?
- Yeah, that's how it ended up.

139
00:10:35,632 --> 00:10:37,824
- Dr. Mi Hyun, could you come here?
- Yeah, I'm coming.

140
00:10:37,824 --> 00:10:38,905
I should get going.

141
00:10:38,905 --> 00:10:39,926
Oh, right!

142
00:10:39,926 --> 00:10:43,607
Grandma Jong Sun will probably
insist on not being admitted again.

143
00:10:43,607 --> 00:10:45,067
Please try to talk her into it.

144
00:10:45,067 --> 00:10:46,787
- I should get going.
- Yeah.

145
00:10:46,787 --> 00:10:48,921
- Good work!
- Yeah.

146
00:10:50,868 --> 00:10:55,338
Jin Su and... Mi Hyun?

147
00:10:56,909 --> 00:10:58,197
[High-Value Donor Club Members' Day]
<i>Next,</i>

148
00:10:58,197 --> 00:11:01,085
<i>we will present this year's
Community Contribution Award.</i>

149
00:11:01,085 --> 00:11:03,435
<i>Congratulations, Mr. Mok Gong Eui.</i>

150
00:11:03,435 --> 00:11:05,417
<i>Please give a big round of applause.</i>

151
00:11:05,417 --> 00:11:09,878
[Sim Yu Geon]

152
00:11:09,878 --> 00:11:13,335
What? Why isn't there even a profile?

153
00:11:13,335 --> 00:11:16,585
Hey, what are you doing? Everyone's watching.

154
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:20,965
How much longer is left on my contract?

155
00:11:20,965 --> 00:11:24,111
Why does that matter?
You're doing it either way.

156
00:11:24,111 --> 00:11:28,571
Stop worrying about other things
and focus on your meeting with Director Kim.

157
00:11:29,225 --> 00:11:31,991
I don't know anything.

158
00:11:31,991 --> 00:11:34,178
Before I knew it, my contract had been renewed,

159
00:11:34,178 --> 00:11:35,738
and my next project was already lined up.

160
00:11:35,738 --> 00:11:39,057
How easy is that? You just take
whatever you're given.

161
00:11:39,057 --> 00:11:42,984
Oh, sometimes I wish I were my own daughter.

162
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:47,290
Mom.

163
00:11:47,911 --> 00:11:52,802
You may not have raised a child yourself,
but you've played plenty of mothers.

164
00:11:52,802 --> 00:11:57,554
If you force it in before it's digested,
the baby will just throw it up.

165
00:11:57,554 --> 00:11:59,469
What do you mean?

166
00:11:59,469 --> 00:12:04,336
<i>Next, we'd like to invite Ms. An Su Hui,
CEO of Topline Entertainment.</i>

167
00:12:04,336 --> 00:12:06,256
<i>- A big round of applause, please.</i>
- We'll talk later.

168
00:12:06,256 --> 00:12:09,563
<i>Ms. An Su Hui, who has been a consistent donor,</i>

169
00:12:09,563 --> 00:12:12,923
<i>will also serve as a club ambassador
moving forward.</i>

170
00:12:12,923 --> 00:12:14,795
Thank you.

171
00:12:14,795 --> 00:12:19,343
There are so many people here
who've contributed far more than I have,

172
00:12:19,343 --> 00:12:23,728
so I'm humbled to receive this award.

173
00:12:23,728 --> 00:12:28,849
Actually, I think the reason I've been
able to keep donating for almost ten years

174
00:12:28,849 --> 00:12:34,041
is because of my daughter, Ha Na,
who came here with me today.

175
00:12:34,041 --> 00:12:36,941
Ha Na, thank you.

176
00:12:54,265 --> 00:12:56,399
Ha Na was actually filming today.

177
00:12:56,399 --> 00:13:00,097
She just stopped by for a moment
to congratulate me on my award.

178
00:13:00,097 --> 00:13:02,971
Ha Na is so kind, isn't she?

179
00:13:02,971 --> 00:13:05,217
Well, going forward...

180
00:13:08,431 --> 00:13:11,458
- Hello, I've brought your laundry.
- Oh.

181
00:13:11,458 --> 00:13:13,418
Sir, I'm so sorry,

182
00:13:13,418 --> 00:13:17,368
but they say there's a stain on the shirt
that won't come out.

183
00:13:17,368 --> 00:13:19,632
That's okay. Thank you.

184
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:21,593
Thank you.

185
00:13:45,387 --> 00:13:47,956
<i>Don't worry! Laundry service. Sorry!</i>

186
00:13:47,956 --> 00:13:49,416
<i>Excuse me.</i>

187
00:13:49,416 --> 00:13:53,026
<i>Would you go out with me?</i>

188
00:14:06,007 --> 00:14:08,976
Why are you drinking this much
in broad daylight?

189
00:14:08,976 --> 00:14:11,513
Time doesn't matter.

190
00:14:11,513 --> 00:14:14,946
If I get off work in the morning,
I'll just drink in the morning.

191
00:14:14,946 --> 00:14:17,028
Ah... that brings back memories.

192
00:14:17,028 --> 00:14:18,041
Hey!

193
00:14:18,041 --> 00:14:22,146
Find someone new before you turn 30.

194
00:14:22,146 --> 00:14:24,773
This is a great opportunity.

195
00:14:24,773 --> 00:14:27,773
Even if you don't meet your match,
at least the shopping mall promotion will work.

196
00:14:27,773 --> 00:14:31,159
Still... how can you ask me
to go on a dating show?

197
00:14:31,159 --> 00:14:34,074
Are you still not over me?

198
00:14:34,074 --> 00:14:38,547
We only dated for three months,
and we've been broken up for over three years.

199
00:14:38,547 --> 00:14:40,114
That's harsh, Sa Rang.

200
00:14:40,114 --> 00:14:42,799
Just do it once, please.

201
00:14:43,647 --> 00:14:47,933
Please come on our show, Love Chain, just once.

202
00:14:51,825 --> 00:14:53,653
Who is this?

203
00:14:54,741 --> 00:14:56,522
Hello?

204
00:14:56,522 --> 00:14:57,978
<i>This is Seo In Uk.</i>

205
00:14:57,978 --> 00:14:59,660
Pardon? Who?

206
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:00,922
<i>We met at the hotel.</i>

207
00:15:00,922 --> 00:15:04,461
<i>- The shirt... the lipstick.</i>
- Pardon?

208
00:15:04,461 --> 00:15:06,879
I'm the guy you asked out.

209
00:15:07,668 --> 00:15:10,929
<i>Would you go out with me?</i>

210
00:15:10,929 --> 00:15:12,737
<i>Yes, baby?</i>

211
00:15:13,788 --> 00:15:15,372
Who is it?

212
00:15:15,372 --> 00:15:16,710
Hey, you should go.

213
00:15:16,710 --> 00:15:18,964
- Huh?
- I said go!

214
00:15:22,005 --> 00:15:25,200
Choi Sa Rang. Don't ever call me again.

215
00:15:29,487 --> 00:15:31,675
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Yes.

216
00:15:31,675 --> 00:15:33,682
<i>Want to come?</i>

217
00:15:44,598 --> 00:15:47,195
It's still early evening. Is that okay?

218
00:15:47,195 --> 00:15:48,792
Of course.

219
00:15:53,438 --> 00:15:57,224
Should I keep you company, or...

220
00:15:57,224 --> 00:15:59,310
get drunk with you?

221
00:16:01,858 --> 00:16:03,568
Get drunk.

222
00:16:10,804 --> 00:16:13,260
Something with a clean acidity

223
00:16:13,260 --> 00:16:16,719
and a distinct mineral water-like clarity...

224
00:16:16,719 --> 00:16:19,980
I'd like a bottle of
Dolcetto di Vigna 2014, please.

225
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,734
Thank you very much.

226
00:16:23,746 --> 00:16:26,412
I'm not sure when it started, but...

227
00:16:26,412 --> 00:16:28,059
suddenly drinks just go down way too easily.

228
00:16:28,059 --> 00:16:30,685
- The chicken suddenly flapped and flew off.
- Jeez...

229
00:16:30,685 --> 00:16:31,926
That's what I figured.

230
00:16:31,926 --> 00:16:33,932
That's right.

231
00:16:36,374 --> 00:16:38,803
So this was all a casting call
for a dating show?

232
00:16:38,803 --> 00:16:40,667
And you're Writer Choi Sa Rang?

233
00:16:40,667 --> 00:16:45,422
Yep! Our producer also did "Crazy in Love."

234
00:16:45,422 --> 00:16:48,696
You know it, right?
It was the No. 1 trending show!

235
00:16:48,696 --> 00:16:50,415
Never heard of it.

236
00:16:51,016 --> 00:16:53,809
But... is this how you
usually recruit contestants?

237
00:16:53,809 --> 00:16:57,710
No, normally we take applications
or reach out through DMs...

238
00:16:57,710 --> 00:17:01,104
but you and I are... how should I put it?

239
00:17:01,104 --> 00:17:03,389
Maybe fate?

240
00:17:06,662 --> 00:17:09,696
If I join, does that mean I'll keep seeing you?

241
00:17:09,696 --> 00:17:13,819
Of course. We'll be stuck together
for two whole weeks.

242
00:17:13,819 --> 00:17:16,603
- What if I don't?
- This will be the last time, right?

243
00:17:16,603 --> 00:17:21,340
Oh, that would be... a shame.

244
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:01,632
Why did you call me?

245
00:18:02,588 --> 00:18:04,948
I was curious.

246
00:18:04,948 --> 00:18:07,821
A woman who asked me out the first time we met.

247
00:18:07,821 --> 00:18:09,775
I was curious too.

248
00:18:09,775 --> 00:18:12,523
What you'd be like in a relationship.

249
00:18:27,410 --> 00:18:30,501
Wow, Woo Soo Bin... what is he trying to do?

250
00:18:30,501 --> 00:18:33,232
What time does he think it is?

251
00:18:36,401 --> 00:18:39,440
Hey! Where are you?
Do you know how many times I called?

252
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:41,912
If you're going somewhere
or coming back late, you have to tell me!

253
00:18:41,912 --> 00:18:43,549
We agreed we'd share everything!

254
00:18:43,549 --> 00:18:45,009
<i>Sorry.</i>

255
00:18:45,009 --> 00:18:47,413
<i>Grandma Jong Sun collapsed,</i>

256
00:18:47,413 --> 00:18:49,028
<i>so I had to bring her to the hospital.</i>

257
00:18:49,028 --> 00:18:51,594
What? Is she okay?

258
00:18:51,594 --> 00:18:54,260
<i>She hurt her back a little.</i>

259
00:18:54,260 --> 00:18:57,942
<i>They want to admit her and run some tests.</i>

260
00:18:59,454 --> 00:19:01,282
Sorry...

261
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:06,190
but you'll have to work alone tonight.

262
00:19:06,190 --> 00:19:09,990
<i>Oh, you're not coming back tonight then?</i>

263
00:19:09,990 --> 00:19:11,777
I'm not sure.

264
00:19:11,777 --> 00:19:13,991
<i>Which hospital are you at?</i>

265
00:19:17,574 --> 00:19:19,630
My father's hospital.

266
00:19:54,256 --> 00:19:55,569
Yeah.

267
00:19:55,569 --> 00:19:59,036
I'm stopping by Grandma's place
to grab a few things.

268
00:19:59,036 --> 00:20:02,129
You left in such a hurry,
you probably didn't bring anything.

269
00:20:02,129 --> 00:20:04,010
Yeah.

270
00:20:04,010 --> 00:20:05,790
What room is she in?

271
00:20:07,228 --> 00:20:10,084
- Hey, hey! Did you hear about it?
- What is it?

272
00:20:10,084 --> 00:20:12,796
I heard Director Ian
is our hospital director's son.

273
00:20:12,796 --> 00:20:14,616
- Really?
- Yeah!

274
00:20:14,616 --> 00:20:17,564
- Good afternoon.
- Good afternoon.

275
00:20:22,113 --> 00:20:24,227
- What's going on?
- Oh.

276
00:20:24,227 --> 00:20:27,591
I think it's because of your son.

277
00:20:28,695 --> 00:20:31,806
- My son? Why?
- He came by yesterday.

278
00:20:31,806 --> 00:20:36,945
Word spread in no time
that Director Ian is your son.

279
00:20:36,945 --> 00:20:40,658
Honestly, if you've got such an amazing son,

280
00:20:40,658 --> 00:20:42,826
you're allowed to brag about it
at least once, aren't you?

281
00:20:42,826 --> 00:20:46,538
I would've put him in the hospital promo video

282
00:20:46,538 --> 00:20:49,685
and plastered his photos everywhere by now.

283
00:20:49,685 --> 00:20:51,512
Congratulations.

284
00:20:52,469 --> 00:20:54,389
Well, I'm proud of him.

285
00:20:54,389 --> 00:20:58,838
But it's not something to make
such a big deal out of, you know.

286
00:20:59,478 --> 00:21:01,971
Just let it pass quietly.

287
00:21:01,971 --> 00:21:05,754
He doesn't like unnecessary attention.

288
00:21:05,754 --> 00:21:07,260
Yes, sir.

289
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:11,188
By the way...

290
00:21:11,188 --> 00:21:14,056
why did he come to the hospital?

291
00:21:22,179 --> 00:21:24,776
Mrs. Park Jong Sun?

292
00:21:24,776 --> 00:21:28,798
- Oh, my. Oh, my.
- Oh, no need to get up.

293
00:21:30,032 --> 00:21:32,094
How are you feeling?

294
00:21:32,094 --> 00:21:35,628
Well, I'm fine.

295
00:21:35,628 --> 00:21:41,045
Oh, my. You didn't have to come
all the way here when you must be so busy.

296
00:21:41,045 --> 00:21:43,899
I heard my son was well
taken care of at your home.

297
00:21:43,899 --> 00:21:45,580
I couldn't just do nothing.

298
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:47,712
Oh, not at all.

299
00:21:47,712 --> 00:21:50,357
I was the one who was helped by Soo Bin.

300
00:21:50,357 --> 00:21:52,578
Oh, is that so?

301
00:21:52,578 --> 00:21:56,285
Oh... by the way, where's Soo Bin?

302
00:21:56,285 --> 00:21:59,319
Yi Jae said she was coming,
so I think Soo Bin went to pick her up.

303
00:21:59,319 --> 00:22:01,505
Oh, I see...

304
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:05,712
I'll make sure you're well taken care of.

305
00:22:05,712 --> 00:22:08,127
Oh, thank you so much.

306
00:22:19,830 --> 00:22:21,859
<i>The door is opening.</i>

307
00:23:26,428 --> 00:23:29,014
<i>I'm sorry!</i>

308
00:23:30,235 --> 00:23:33,496
<i>Please forgive me just this once.</i>

309
00:23:36,614 --> 00:23:38,465
<i>Stand up!</i>

310
00:23:42,191 --> 00:23:46,476
<i>Please forgive me just this once... please.</i>

311
00:24:00,778 --> 00:24:04,206
If you meant to cut blood ties,

312
00:24:05,153 --> 00:24:08,894
you should've gone farther.
Somewhere far beyond my reach.

313
00:24:08,894 --> 00:24:12,605
Instead, you only came this far?

314
00:24:12,605 --> 00:24:15,309
I left so I could come back...

315
00:24:16,611 --> 00:24:19,046
so I wouldn't run away anymore.

316
00:24:23,926 --> 00:24:25,717
[Registration & Billing]
[Outpatient Clinic]

317
00:24:41,874 --> 00:24:43,973
Oh, come on...

318
00:25:12,262 --> 00:25:14,189
It's okay...

319
00:25:14,806 --> 00:25:16,455
You're okay.

320
00:25:18,720 --> 00:25:20,590
You're okay...

321
00:26:20,010 --> 00:26:22,629
I'm here, Woo Soo Bin.

322
00:26:25,618 --> 00:26:28,012
You don't have to come out.

323
00:26:28,012 --> 00:26:31,400
I just... wanted you to know I'm here.

324
00:26:44,167 --> 00:26:48,039
- Ju Yi Jae, about earlier...
- I heard you met Mi Hyun.

325
00:26:49,496 --> 00:26:53,024
I haven't seen her since her wedding either.

326
00:26:53,024 --> 00:26:55,831
I even filmed their wedding video.

327
00:26:58,198 --> 00:27:00,245
Yeah?

328
00:27:00,245 --> 00:27:03,430
It's probably been three years already.

329
00:27:03,430 --> 00:27:05,282
I think I still have that video.

330
00:27:05,282 --> 00:27:07,407
I'll show you next time.

331
00:27:08,460 --> 00:27:10,923
Seong Chan must have grown a lot.

332
00:27:10,923 --> 00:27:13,302
How old is he now?

333
00:27:14,296 --> 00:27:16,623
Maybe he starts school next year?

334
00:27:18,337 --> 00:27:20,379
You said they got married three years ago.

335
00:27:20,379 --> 00:27:22,810
Oh, they had the baby first.

336
00:27:22,810 --> 00:27:25,595
You'd know right away he's Jin Su's son.

337
00:27:25,595 --> 00:27:28,340
He's basically Kim Jin Su Junior.

338
00:27:29,610 --> 00:27:32,242
Oh, right! I heard this today too.

339
00:27:32,242 --> 00:27:33,991
You know Kim Jin Su...

340
00:27:33,991 --> 00:27:37,655
He quit his perfectly good job
and writes web novels now.

341
00:27:37,655 --> 00:27:40,585
What was his pen name again?

342
00:27:40,585 --> 00:27:42,608
"Ode to Jin Su?"

343
00:27:42,608 --> 00:27:47,584
Oh, the name sounds grand,
but apparently the income isn't much.

344
00:27:47,584 --> 00:27:52,753
Still, he handles housework and childcare
without a word, so she just lets him be.

345
00:27:55,666 --> 00:27:57,588
That's so Jin Su.

346
00:28:04,929 --> 00:28:07,129
Thank you, Ju Yi Jae.

347
00:28:38,709 --> 00:28:40,334
[The female lead is disappointing]
[Oh Ha Na and rom-coms do NOT mix. She's so awkward]

348
00:28:40,334 --> 00:28:41,724
[Sang Yeon is hard-carrying this show]
[There's zero chemistry]

349
00:28:41,724 --> 00:28:43,530
[Romance? More like a thriller]
[Why does she look so serious in a rom-com?]

350
00:28:47,500 --> 00:28:51,266
Ha Na, stop reading the comments.

351
00:28:53,513 --> 00:28:55,163
Do I really look that bad to you?

352
00:28:55,163 --> 00:28:56,952
Bad? Not at all!

353
00:28:56,952 --> 00:29:00,472
You're just overshadowed by your looks,
but you're totally an acting powerhouse.

354
00:29:00,472 --> 00:29:03,577
You've played killers, demons,
detectives, judges...

355
00:29:03,577 --> 00:29:06,208
You're good at playing
both good guys and bad guys.

356
00:29:06,208 --> 00:29:09,321
Then why does everyone go crazy
whenever I do romance?

357
00:29:09,321 --> 00:29:13,594
Maybe it's because you've never been in love?

358
00:29:15,134 --> 00:29:18,723
By that logic, I must have
killed someone before.

359
00:29:18,723 --> 00:29:20,576
Have you?

360
00:29:21,945 --> 00:29:26,224
Oh, Ha Na... just kidding, just kidding!

361
00:29:33,319 --> 00:29:34,821
Ha Na.

362
00:29:35,482 --> 00:29:39,986
People who are in love show it on their faces.

363
00:29:39,986 --> 00:29:44,952
Their eyes, nose, and lips
all turn toward that person.

364
00:29:44,952 --> 00:29:47,192
You can't hide it.

365
00:30:01,927 --> 00:30:04,129
Please turn the car around.

366
00:30:06,495 --> 00:30:07,973
Welcome.

367
00:30:07,973 --> 00:30:09,918
Welcome.

368
00:30:15,823 --> 00:30:18,670
Would you like to order
when your party arrives?

369
00:30:19,322 --> 00:30:21,079
One serving of meat, please.

370
00:30:21,079 --> 00:30:23,540
Orders start from two servings.

371
00:30:27,583 --> 00:30:29,081
What brings you here?

372
00:30:29,081 --> 00:30:32,559
Well... I wanted to ride a motorcycle.

373
00:30:34,137 --> 00:30:36,086
When do you get off work?

374
00:30:36,086 --> 00:30:39,431
I've got about an hour left.

375
00:30:40,299 --> 00:30:42,106
I'll wait.

376
00:30:42,838 --> 00:30:44,318
Yes.

377
00:30:49,099 --> 00:30:51,258
<i>Thank you.</i>

378
00:30:51,258 --> 00:30:53,058
<i>It's so pretty.</i>

379
00:31:00,666 --> 00:31:05,352
Honestly, who would turn Oh Ha Na down
if she asked them out?

380
00:31:05,352 --> 00:31:06,825
Me.

381
00:31:06,825 --> 00:31:09,161
But is she really forever single?

382
00:31:09,161 --> 00:31:11,121
Does that even make sense?

383
00:31:11,121 --> 00:31:14,249
That's why people say she can't do romance.

384
00:31:14,249 --> 00:31:17,267
Even if she dated someone,
wouldn't she be boring?

385
00:31:17,267 --> 00:31:20,130
Hey, hey! Just look at those eyes.

386
00:31:20,130 --> 00:31:23,103
Come on, how can you say that
after seeing those eyes?

387
00:31:23,103 --> 00:31:27,858
- She looks like she'd ruin a man's life.
- That's right.

388
00:31:27,858 --> 00:31:30,077
Who was that? Oh, An Su Hui!

389
00:31:30,077 --> 00:31:32,924
She divorced her husband
as soon as his business went under.

390
00:31:32,924 --> 00:31:35,229
She was living like a lady of leisure
thanks to her husband before that.

391
00:31:35,229 --> 00:31:38,350
Oh my... she's so cold-hearted.

392
00:31:38,350 --> 00:31:42,486
Well, they say daughters take after
their mothers' fate. Blood is blood, after all.

393
00:31:42,486 --> 00:31:44,397
Well, like mother, like daughter.

394
00:31:44,397 --> 00:31:47,995
- Oh, my. You startled me.
- Darn, you're really loud.

395
00:31:52,202 --> 00:31:53,564
Boss, I'm quitting.

396
00:31:53,564 --> 00:31:55,207
Hey! What?

397
00:31:55,207 --> 00:31:57,861
- What is it?
- Hey, hey, hey!

398
00:32:04,925 --> 00:32:06,918
Why couldn't you say anything?

399
00:32:07,816 --> 00:32:11,670
You meddle in my life so well.

400
00:32:12,432 --> 00:32:15,212
Why run from your own?

401
00:32:16,478 --> 00:32:18,081
Why?

402
00:32:22,010 --> 00:32:23,929
It's okay.

403
00:32:24,986 --> 00:32:27,598
Those people are just...

404
00:32:27,598 --> 00:32:30,400
people who are allowed to say things like that.

405
00:32:32,448 --> 00:32:35,052
And I'm just... someone people can criticize.

406
00:32:49,913 --> 00:32:51,394
Get on.

407
00:32:52,104 --> 00:32:54,713
You came here to ride a motorcycle, didn't you?

408
00:33:56,041 --> 00:33:57,813
Thanks.

409
00:34:03,961 --> 00:34:06,425
But why aren't you asking?

410
00:34:06,425 --> 00:34:08,878
How could I even know
where you were and find you?

411
00:34:10,717 --> 00:34:14,070
I didn't think this was the right time to ask.

412
00:34:14,939 --> 00:34:16,712
And...

413
00:34:16,712 --> 00:34:19,155
I figured you wouldn't answer anyway.

414
00:34:19,155 --> 00:34:21,480
I searched for you.

415
00:34:23,405 --> 00:34:26,817
But what kind of actor
doesn't even have a profile?

416
00:34:26,817 --> 00:34:29,685
Then where did you see me?

417
00:34:29,685 --> 00:34:31,765
On social media.

418
00:34:32,656 --> 00:34:37,057
When I searched your name,
some web dramas came up,

419
00:34:37,057 --> 00:34:40,044
and there were also photos of you serving
at a barbecue restaurant.

420
00:34:40,044 --> 00:34:43,539
- They were all taken without permission.
- Oh...

421
00:34:43,539 --> 00:34:46,044
Should I sue them for you?

422
00:34:46,044 --> 00:34:47,784
I'm fine.

423
00:34:49,766 --> 00:34:52,775
But why did you search for me?

424
00:34:56,306 --> 00:35:00,042
Well, you know... it's unfair.

425
00:35:00,042 --> 00:35:03,938
We're friends, but I'm the only one
who doesn't know much about you.

426
00:35:03,938 --> 00:35:06,317
You searched for me too, didn't you?

427
00:35:06,317 --> 00:35:09,177
If you search for Oh Ha Na,
even my fortune reading comes up.

428
00:35:09,177 --> 00:35:11,757
It says I'll make a ton of money.

429
00:35:13,572 --> 00:35:15,760
But apparently...

430
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:18,133
I'm destined to be lonely forever.

431
00:35:21,948 --> 00:35:24,294
I haven't searched you.

432
00:35:25,401 --> 00:35:29,310
Usually, friends just ask each other directly.

433
00:35:33,901 --> 00:35:36,090
Oh...

434
00:35:36,090 --> 00:35:38,537
I'm Sim Yu Geon,

435
00:35:39,355 --> 00:35:41,616
and I'm 29 years old.

436
00:35:42,340 --> 00:35:44,036
And then?

437
00:35:44,036 --> 00:35:48,245
My family is just my father and me.

438
00:35:49,518 --> 00:35:52,211
And my hobby is...

439
00:35:52,211 --> 00:35:54,207
watching Hong Kong movies?

440
00:35:56,951 --> 00:35:59,870
My reason for wanting to become an actor was...

441
00:35:59,870 --> 00:36:04,194
simply because Kaneshiro Takeshi was so cool.

442
00:36:04,194 --> 00:36:06,068
<i>- Dad!
- What?</i>

443
00:36:06,068 --> 00:36:10,192
<i>I've made my decision, and I, Sim Yu Geon,
will become Korea's Kaneshiro Takeshi.</i>

444
00:36:10,192 --> 00:36:11,755
<i>I've made up my mind too.</i>

445
00:36:11,755 --> 00:36:15,139
<i>I'm going to scoop you up
with this net, you punk!</i>

446
00:36:15,139 --> 00:36:16,160
<i>So cold, so cold!</i>

447
00:36:16,160 --> 00:36:19,304
My favorite movie has always been
"Chungking Express."

448
00:36:19,304 --> 00:36:21,743
My favorite dialogue is...

449
00:36:26,812 --> 00:36:29,699
"If love had an expiration date...

450
00:36:30,656 --> 00:36:35,237
I want my love to last for ten thousand years."

451
00:36:35,237 --> 00:36:37,138
That's the line.

452
00:36:37,733 --> 00:36:40,683
<i>What? You want to break up?
How can you leave me?</i>

453
00:36:40,683 --> 00:36:44,674
It started with "I want to
become Kaneshiro Takeshi,"

454
00:36:44,674 --> 00:36:48,561
but at some point it became "I want to act."

455
00:36:48,561 --> 00:36:53,795
[First Audition for the film "Alley Story"]

456
00:36:53,795 --> 00:36:56,135
<i>Director! Director!</i>

457
00:36:56,135 --> 00:37:00,059
<i>Yeah, thanks for your hard work.
You can go now.</i>

458
00:37:00,059 --> 00:37:02,365
<i>- Oh...
- Who approved him?</i>

459
00:37:02,365 --> 00:37:04,452
<i>- Thank you for your hard work.
- Thank you for your hard work.</i>

460
00:37:04,452 --> 00:37:08,478
<i>- Next, Mr. Han Dong Min! Please go in.
- Next, next!</i>

461
00:37:08,478 --> 00:37:12,357
But even getting the chance
to audition wasn't easy.

462
00:37:12,357 --> 00:37:15,510
<i>That's it. Come on. Get in here.
Take your best shot.</i>

463
00:37:17,531 --> 00:37:20,908
<i>Hold on, hold on. Hey, what's wrong with this?</i>

464
00:37:20,908 --> 00:37:22,764
<i>- Director Choi!
- Yeah.</i>

465
00:37:22,764 --> 00:37:25,112
<i>That's real, isn't it? Give it to me.</i>

466
00:37:25,112 --> 00:37:27,183
<i>No, sir. This is dangerous...</i>

467
00:37:27,183 --> 00:37:31,736
<i>Hey, can't you see it? Their eyes have changed.</i>

468
00:37:32,586 --> 00:37:34,709
<i>Let's go with this.</i>

469
00:37:34,709 --> 00:37:38,609
<i>Ready... action!</i>

470
00:37:38,609 --> 00:37:41,709
<i>- Hiyah!
- It's done!</i>

471
00:37:44,411 --> 00:37:46,012
<i>Hah!</i>

472
00:37:48,576 --> 00:37:53,754
Maybe I might never have my name called
even once in my whole life.

473
00:37:58,003 --> 00:38:02,890
But still, if my dream had an expiration date,

474
00:38:02,890 --> 00:38:05,183
I'd want it to last for ten thousand years.

475
00:38:06,203 --> 00:38:08,483
My dad told me,

476
00:38:08,483 --> 00:38:13,369
"If you don't make it in ten years,
come back home."

477
00:38:15,698 --> 00:38:18,498
But somehow, ten years have passed.

478
00:38:20,258 --> 00:38:22,425
And I still haven't become anything.

479
00:38:24,524 --> 00:38:27,350
What does "making it" even mean?

480
00:38:27,350 --> 00:38:30,019
Who decides that?

481
00:38:31,186 --> 00:38:33,661
Just go back home.

482
00:38:33,661 --> 00:38:37,202
See your dad and come back.

483
00:38:38,138 --> 00:38:41,488
- That's not what he meant...
- I know.

484
00:38:41,488 --> 00:38:43,392
But...

485
00:38:43,392 --> 00:38:46,738
I don't think those words only sound cold.

486
00:38:47,705 --> 00:38:51,322
It feels like he's saying
you can always come back.

487
00:38:52,302 --> 00:38:56,192
It feels like a warm parent's embrace...

488
00:38:57,173 --> 00:38:59,378
I'm so jealous.

489
00:39:00,413 --> 00:39:02,860
You're jealous?

490
00:39:04,420 --> 00:39:06,407
Well...

491
00:39:07,028 --> 00:39:13,028
Want to hear a story about Oh Ha Na
that you won't find online?

492
00:39:23,236 --> 00:39:24,258
<i>Is it fun?</i>

493
00:39:24,258 --> 00:39:27,812
When I was little, I liked being on TV.

494
00:39:27,812 --> 00:39:30,920
<i>Mom's going to make you pretty...</i>

495
00:39:30,920 --> 00:39:32,749
<i>You're pretty.</i>

496
00:39:37,726 --> 00:39:40,954
<i>Ma'am, I have an overnight shoot.
Please stay until tomorrow morning.</i>

497
00:39:40,954 --> 00:39:42,865
<i>Yes, of course. Have a good day.</i>

498
00:39:42,865 --> 00:39:44,735
<i>Mom!</i>

499
00:39:51,183 --> 00:39:53,388
<i>Shall we watch TV?</i>

500
00:39:53,388 --> 00:39:54,439
<i>Yeah.</i>

501
00:39:54,439 --> 00:39:58,523
<i>- Who does Ha Na take after to be this pretty?
- You, Mom.</i>

502
00:39:58,523 --> 00:40:00,204
- I was happier in that world.
<i>- What is your name?</i>

503
00:40:00,204 --> 00:40:01,823
<i>Oh Ha Na!</i>

504
00:40:01,823 --> 00:40:03,890
I didn't even know it was fake.

505
00:40:03,890 --> 00:40:06,173
<i>- Yeah, yeah. Our Ha Na's the prettiest.
- Ready...</i>

506
00:40:06,173 --> 00:40:07,324
<i>Action!</i>

507
00:40:07,324 --> 00:40:11,328
<i>- Ha Na's milk is unique. There's only one.
- Can you smile a little brighter?</i>

508
00:40:11,328 --> 00:40:14,206
<i>- Ha Na's milk is unique. There's only one.
- Let's make it a bit prettier.</i>

509
00:40:14,206 --> 00:40:19,044
<i>- Hana's milk is unique. There's only one.
- Let's try again.</i>

510
00:40:19,044 --> 00:40:21,564
<i>Cut! NG!</i>

511
00:40:23,679 --> 00:40:25,581
<i>- Ugh...
- Please give Ha Na some water.</i>

512
00:40:25,581 --> 00:40:28,847
<i>Stop making such a fuss. You'll spoil her.</i>

513
00:40:30,372 --> 00:40:31,929
<i>Ha Na.</i>

514
00:40:31,929 --> 00:40:35,266
<i>What's wrong with you?
Are you going to disappoint Mom?</i>

515
00:40:36,917 --> 00:40:38,608
<i>Smile.</i>

516
00:40:40,796 --> 00:40:43,706
<i>That's it. Our Ha Na is ready.</i>

517
00:40:50,397 --> 00:40:52,150
[Who's Your Partner? Ha Na's High School]

518
00:40:52,150 --> 00:40:54,744
<i>Ha Na's High School!</i>

519
00:40:54,744 --> 00:40:56,582
<i>Ha Na!</i>

520
00:40:56,582 --> 00:40:58,166
<i>Good morning!</i>

521
00:40:58,166 --> 00:41:01,844
<i>I heard you were filming late again yesterday.
Aren't you tired?</i>

522
00:41:01,844 --> 00:41:03,755
<i>I'm fine.</i>

523
00:41:03,755 --> 00:41:06,965
<i>Our Ha Na is amazing, right?
She's perfect at everything.</i>

524
00:41:06,965 --> 00:41:09,219
<i>I almost envy her.</i>

525
00:41:09,219 --> 00:41:11,601
But I eventually realized it...

526
00:41:11,601 --> 00:41:13,211
<i>- Thank you.
- Thank you.</i>

527
00:41:13,211 --> 00:41:15,578
- that my whole world was fake.
<i>- Don't forget about the homework.</i>

528
00:41:15,578 --> 00:41:17,811
<i>- Yes!
- Yes!</i>

529
00:41:17,811 --> 00:41:19,710
<i>When should we do
the performance assessment together?</i>

530
00:41:19,710 --> 00:41:21,584
<i>- Cut!
- Tomorrow?</i>

531
00:41:21,584 --> 00:41:22,880
<i>Ha Na, good work today.</i>

532
00:41:22,880 --> 00:41:24,792
<i>- See you at the next shoot.
- Yes.</i>

533
00:41:24,792 --> 00:41:26,270
<i>Thank you for your hard work.</i>

534
00:41:26,270 --> 00:41:28,435
<i>- Great work today.
- Good work!</i>

535
00:41:28,435 --> 00:41:31,136
<i>This is seriously ridiculous.</i>

536
00:41:31,136 --> 00:41:33,028
<i>When is this shoot going to end, Ha Na?</i>

537
00:41:33,028 --> 00:41:35,350
<i>Sorry. It ends next week.</i>

538
00:41:35,350 --> 00:41:37,851
<i>I can't stand this whole
"acting close" thing anymore.</i>

539
00:41:37,851 --> 00:41:41,857
<i>- You were the one dying to get on TV.
- That's crazy.</i>

540
00:41:41,857 --> 00:41:44,521
<i>Guys, I'll get going first.</i>

541
00:41:44,521 --> 00:41:46,633
<i>Bye.</i>

542
00:41:46,633 --> 00:41:48,469
<i>Hey, that's enough.</i>

543
00:41:48,469 --> 00:41:50,637
<i>The news about her parents' divorce
came out today.</i>

544
00:41:50,637 --> 00:41:53,347
<i>Wow... I actually have something
Oh Ha Na doesn't?</i>

545
00:41:53,347 --> 00:41:56,363
<i>A happy, loving family?</i>

546
00:41:57,021 --> 00:41:59,090
<i>Huh? It's Oh Ha Na!</i>

547
00:41:59,090 --> 00:42:02,186
<i>- Please move back.
- Did you know about your parents' divorce?</i>

548
00:42:04,357 --> 00:42:06,589
<i>What are your future plans?</i>

549
00:42:21,598 --> 00:42:24,150
<i>- Ah!
- Ah...</i>

550
00:42:24,150 --> 00:42:27,545
<i>Director, you're starting a new project, right?</i>

551
00:42:27,545 --> 00:42:29,297
<i>- What is this?
- Ha Na...</i>

552
00:42:29,297 --> 00:42:31,343
<i>needs to move past her child actor image.</i>

553
00:42:31,343 --> 00:42:34,886
<i>Please spare me some time. I'll come see you.</i>

554
00:42:34,886 --> 00:42:36,470
<i>Me?</i>

555
00:42:37,659 --> 00:42:39,935
<i>I left the set a long time ago.</i>

556
00:42:39,935 --> 00:42:43,728
<i>Right now, I'm busy taking care of Ha Na.
I don't even have time to think.</i>

557
00:42:43,728 --> 00:42:45,602
[Public Culture & Arts Management Agency
Topline Entertainment]

558
00:42:45,602 --> 00:42:48,240
<i>Shall I produce that project?</i>

559
00:42:48,240 --> 00:42:54,051
To someone else, my world
might look beautiful and sparkling.

560
00:42:54,051 --> 00:42:56,199
- But to me...
<i>- Yes.</i>

561
00:42:56,199 --> 00:42:58,890
I want to leave this set now.

562
00:42:58,890 --> 00:43:01,356
Like the ending of "The Truman Show."

563
00:43:02,836 --> 00:43:06,821
Looks like you're already ready to break free.

564
00:43:07,621 --> 00:43:10,132
You said you know it's a set, right?

565
00:43:10,132 --> 00:43:13,469
Now, you just need to find the door.

566
00:43:23,429 --> 00:43:25,397
You smiled...

567
00:43:26,242 --> 00:43:28,889
I've never seen you smile before.

568
00:43:29,679 --> 00:43:31,559
Oh...

569
00:43:48,962 --> 00:43:53,408
[Don't get me wrong,
this is for the shirt cleaning fee]

570
00:44:03,884 --> 00:44:05,771
<i>Are you leaving?</i>

571
00:44:06,394 --> 00:44:08,325
<i>I had a good time.</i>

572
00:44:08,325 --> 00:44:10,583
<i>I'll block your number.</i>

573
00:44:21,107 --> 00:44:22,394
[Writer Choi Sa Rang]

574
00:44:36,106 --> 00:44:37,913
<i>Yeah, In Uk. Did you read all of that?</i>

575
00:44:37,913 --> 00:44:40,678
I slept with a woman a few days ago.

576
00:44:49,046 --> 00:44:51,945
But I can't stop thinking about her.

577
00:44:51,945 --> 00:44:53,918
- Stop or Go?
<i>- Stop!</i>

578
00:44:53,918 --> 00:44:55,428
Okay...

579
00:44:56,391 --> 00:44:57,894
Go!

580
00:45:15,171 --> 00:45:19,244
[HBS, Entertainment Department,
Writer Choi Sa Rang]

581
00:45:19,244 --> 00:45:21,231
What brings you here?

582
00:45:22,165 --> 00:45:24,441
Is Writer Choi Sa Rang here?

583
00:45:24,441 --> 00:45:26,680
Who are you?

584
00:45:28,720 --> 00:45:32,107
I don't know why Writer Choi
didn't say anything.

585
00:45:32,107 --> 00:45:33,820
No!

586
00:45:35,901 --> 00:45:37,164
What do you mean, no?

587
00:45:37,164 --> 00:45:40,183
From head to toe, you're exactly
the type we were looking for.

588
00:45:40,183 --> 00:45:42,646
You said you worked as a producer
in Hollywood for a long time?

589
00:45:42,646 --> 00:45:44,769
And you're currently the CEO of a film company?

590
00:45:44,769 --> 00:45:48,020
- Yes, that's right.
- A smart and sexy man.

591
00:45:48,020 --> 00:45:51,000
- Okay, go!
- Okay, go.

592
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:52,249
No, Producer!

593
00:45:52,249 --> 00:45:55,255
We already finalized the cast.

594
00:45:55,255 --> 00:46:00,162
Sorry, but Mr. Seo In Uk,
all the spots are taken.

595
00:46:00,162 --> 00:46:02,260
A wildcard!

596
00:46:02,260 --> 00:46:03,743
You look like a total wildcard.

597
00:46:03,743 --> 00:46:06,475
Let's introduce you
as a wildcard entry on Day 5.

598
00:46:06,475 --> 00:46:09,228
Call me a wildcard or whatever. I don't care.

599
00:46:09,228 --> 00:46:13,198
Oh, my! You even have a sense of humor.

600
00:46:13,198 --> 00:46:16,485
You're perfect. I really like you.

601
00:46:16,485 --> 00:46:18,815
I slept with this man.

602
00:46:21,329 --> 00:46:23,749
- What?
- I slept with him.

603
00:46:23,749 --> 00:46:25,343
That means it's not okay, right?

604
00:46:25,343 --> 00:46:27,964
I don't think this will work, Mr. Seo In Uk.
Please leave quickly.

605
00:46:27,964 --> 00:46:30,215
Wait, wait, wait!

606
00:46:30,215 --> 00:46:32,128
How many times?

607
00:46:33,226 --> 00:46:35,674
- What?
- How many times did you sleep together?

608
00:46:35,674 --> 00:46:37,799
Once, one-night.

609
00:46:37,799 --> 00:46:39,667
- Do you love him?
- Have I lost my mind?

610
00:46:39,667 --> 00:46:41,982
- Do you love her?
- No!

611
00:46:41,982 --> 00:46:44,333
That's fine then! Let's do it.

612
00:46:44,333 --> 00:46:46,731
- Let's have him on the show!
- Producer!

613
00:46:46,731 --> 00:46:50,027
A guy you had a one-night stand with
is better than your ex-boyfriend.

614
00:46:50,027 --> 00:46:52,159
Right?

615
00:46:52,159 --> 00:46:54,509
- Go!
- Go.

616
00:46:57,103 --> 00:47:00,623
Oh, my... I'm losing it.

617
00:47:01,422 --> 00:47:03,747
[Participation Contract for the HBS
Dating Reality Show "Love Chain"]

618
00:47:06,110 --> 00:47:09,427
- Are you enjoying this situation?
- Yes!

619
00:47:09,427 --> 00:47:13,000
Please say you won't do it, even now. Please?

620
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:17,109
I'll explain everything to the producer.

621
00:47:17,109 --> 00:47:19,004
Why me?

622
00:47:19,004 --> 00:47:22,092
Your ex-boyfriend is okay, but why am I not?

623
00:47:22,092 --> 00:47:25,220
- What, do you like me or something?
- Listen, Mr. Seo In Uk!

624
00:47:25,220 --> 00:47:28,213
I'm the one who blocked you.
You're the one who came after me.

625
00:47:28,213 --> 00:47:29,641
So why did you block me?

626
00:47:29,641 --> 00:47:32,293
It must've been a shame
to end it after just once.

627
00:47:33,455 --> 00:47:34,935
Jeez...

628
00:47:34,935 --> 00:47:36,829
Well, I mean...

629
00:47:36,829 --> 00:47:38,935
how would you even know that yourself?

630
00:47:38,935 --> 00:47:42,060
Did you ask all the women you've slept with?

631
00:47:42,060 --> 00:47:43,833
- So I guess that's a yes?
- No.

632
00:47:43,833 --> 00:47:47,718
No, I mean... do I just sign here?

633
00:47:49,006 --> 00:47:52,021
Are you sure you read through it carefully?

634
00:47:56,903 --> 00:47:58,913
Dating is absolutely not allowed
during filming.

635
00:47:58,913 --> 00:48:01,161
If any damage arises from the relevant facts,

636
00:48:01,161 --> 00:48:04,746
the contract may be terminated
and all appearance fees must be fully refunded.

637
00:48:04,746 --> 00:48:08,944
Not just dating, one-night stands
are included too, of course.

638
00:48:08,944 --> 00:48:11,055
Are you still okay with this?

639
00:48:11,055 --> 00:48:14,817
- You should probably control yourself.
- Control myself?

640
00:48:14,817 --> 00:48:17,550
- What about you, Writer Choi?
- What?

641
00:48:17,550 --> 00:48:19,591
What happens if you date
a cast member during filming?

642
00:48:19,591 --> 00:48:24,088
Sorry, but that's never
going to happen with me.

643
00:48:24,088 --> 00:48:26,668
Especially not with you.

644
00:48:26,668 --> 00:48:30,871
I believe a one-night stand
should stay a one-night stand.

645
00:48:31,578 --> 00:48:33,641
Then, want to bet?

646
00:48:33,641 --> 00:48:37,082
Whether there will be a second time
between us or not.

647
00:48:41,255 --> 00:48:45,246
Her one and only friend died
because of Moo Gyeom.

648
00:48:45,246 --> 00:48:47,650
And you're saying she should tell Moo Gyeom?

649
00:48:47,650 --> 00:48:50,055
Nan Young loves Moo Gyeom.

650
00:48:50,055 --> 00:48:54,309
Why can't you understand that
she's afraid he'll fall apart if she tells him?

651
00:48:54,309 --> 00:48:56,508
She has to bear that pain too.

652
00:48:56,508 --> 00:48:58,904
No matter how noble the reason was,

653
00:48:58,904 --> 00:49:01,817
it's still true that she gave
Nan Young an unforgivable wound.

654
00:49:01,817 --> 00:49:04,223
Then what if Moo Gyeom leaves her?

655
00:49:04,223 --> 00:49:06,848
Then that was all that love was worth.

656
00:49:19,827 --> 00:49:23,005
Can love that can't even bear
that kind of weight...

657
00:49:23,814 --> 00:49:25,549
really last forever?

658
00:49:25,549 --> 00:49:28,634
Then of course, she can't say it.

659
00:49:28,634 --> 00:49:33,242
A love that's more afraid of losing than
willing to promise forever might be

660
00:49:33,242 --> 00:49:35,642
the kind of love that's even bigger.

661
00:49:47,512 --> 00:49:50,620
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

662
00:49:50,620 --> 00:49:51,774
Please enjoy.

663
00:49:51,774 --> 00:49:54,936
[Olive BBQ Chicken Café]

664
00:49:57,995 --> 00:50:02,461
Wow. I still can't believe this pair is real.

665
00:50:02,461 --> 00:50:04,350
Says the one who should talk.

666
00:50:04,350 --> 00:50:06,763
Exactly. I couldn't believe it even
when they said they were dating.

667
00:50:06,763 --> 00:50:09,297
But Mi Hyun waited for him
while he was in the military,

668
00:50:09,297 --> 00:50:11,720
and he helped her study for her exams too.

669
00:50:11,720 --> 00:50:14,689
Yi Jae, you should've stopped me,
even if you had to hit me back then.

670
00:50:14,689 --> 00:50:16,667
- I did.
- Oh, really?

671
00:50:16,667 --> 00:50:18,205
What?

672
00:50:18,851 --> 00:50:20,326
- Honey, where did you get hit?
- Why are you doing this?

673
00:50:20,326 --> 00:50:23,200
- Why are you doing this?
- Ju Yi Jae is pretty strong. How dare you...

674
00:50:23,200 --> 00:50:24,669
Jeez, let go of me!

675
00:50:24,669 --> 00:50:27,152
Wanna get totally wrecked after a long time?

676
00:50:27,152 --> 00:50:30,354
Don't mess with me.
Haven't you seen my muscles?

677
00:50:30,354 --> 00:50:31,835
Where? What muscles are you even talking about?

678
00:50:31,835 --> 00:50:33,155
I can't even show them off...

679
00:50:33,155 --> 00:50:35,382
Honey, tell her about my muscles.

680
00:50:35,382 --> 00:50:38,005
- Where? Where are your muscles?
- It's all muscles right here.

681
00:50:38,005 --> 00:50:40,537
- Do you wanna have it out after a while?
- Wanna go for it?

682
00:50:40,537 --> 00:50:44,527
- Let's see it. Give it a shot.
- Give it a shot. Let's see it.

683
00:50:56,396 --> 00:50:59,303
<i>Mom, shall we have lunch together tomorrow?</i>

684
00:51:23,750 --> 00:51:25,615
You're home?

685
00:51:33,767 --> 00:51:35,588
Right, "Gyeongseong Love Song!"

686
00:51:35,588 --> 00:51:37,890
Wow... hearing that, it just came back to me.

687
00:51:37,890 --> 00:51:41,382
The CSAT was coming up,
but you were still writing that thing, Yi Jae.

688
00:51:41,382 --> 00:51:42,495
Attention!

689
00:51:42,495 --> 00:51:46,379
In my opinion as "Ode to Jin Su,"
I think the story still has some gaps.

690
00:51:46,379 --> 00:51:48,264
I shall fill those gaps myself.

691
00:51:48,264 --> 00:51:52,431
- Shut up. Don't embarrass yourself.
- Why not? Let's hear it.

692
00:51:52,431 --> 00:51:54,437
- Are you serious?
- Yeah.

693
00:51:54,437 --> 00:51:58,303
A protagonist who gives up revenge
for love? Never again!

694
00:51:58,303 --> 00:52:01,145
Our Nan Young will abandon love!

695
00:52:01,145 --> 00:52:03,469
- It's a romance story though?
- Roma...

696
00:52:03,469 --> 00:52:07,109
Shh! Just listen.

697
00:52:07,109 --> 00:52:10,446
The year is 1930, in Gyeongseong.

698
00:52:10,446 --> 00:52:14,931
Urgent footsteps echo through
the deserted streets.

699
00:52:43,020 --> 00:52:45,014
<i>Every night, I swore...</i>

700
00:52:45,014 --> 00:52:48,352
<i>I would end your life with these hands.</i>

701
00:52:48,352 --> 00:52:51,265
<i>But heaven has been cruel.</i>

702
00:52:51,265 --> 00:52:55,487
<i>How is it that these very hands
came to feel your breath instead?</i>

703
00:52:55,487 --> 00:52:59,014
<i>Nan Young... I didn't know.</i>

704
00:52:59,769 --> 00:53:03,323
<i>I didn't know the person who died by my hand
was your precious friend.</i>

705
00:53:03,323 --> 00:53:05,231
<i>Stop making excuses!</i>

706
00:53:05,231 --> 00:53:06,785
Ah... why'd you make her pull a gun?

707
00:53:06,785 --> 00:53:08,513
What's wrong with a gun?

708
00:53:08,513 --> 00:53:10,072
Isn't that kind of random?

709
00:53:10,072 --> 00:53:12,675
So what, is she gonna
get revenge with chopsticks?

710
00:53:12,675 --> 00:53:15,453
Alright, point the gun at him right now!

711
00:53:15,453 --> 00:53:20,660
Cherry blossoms scatter
between the two people standing face-to-face!

712
00:53:22,544 --> 00:53:24,997
- It's winter.
- Oh... is it winter?

713
00:53:24,997 --> 00:53:27,761
- Ugh, jeez...
- Ugh... I really can't stand the cold.

714
00:53:27,761 --> 00:53:31,373
- Come on, can't you do it right?
- Alright, alright. Go on.

715
00:53:31,373 --> 00:53:33,029
Then let snow fall!

716
00:53:33,029 --> 00:53:35,591
Ready... action!

717
00:53:35,591 --> 00:53:38,632
<i>My life belonged to my country anyway.</i>

718
00:53:38,632 --> 00:53:41,125
<i>But if I die by your hand...</i>

719
00:53:41,125 --> 00:53:45,146
<i>I will gladly accept it.</i>

720
00:53:45,146 --> 00:53:48,312
<i>Because you were also my country.</i>

721
00:53:48,312 --> 00:53:51,056
<i>Not a single day passed that I forgot you.</i>

722
00:53:51,747 --> 00:53:53,742
<i>Because I loved you,</i>

723
00:53:54,382 --> 00:53:56,929
<i>I probably won't be able to forget you.</i>

724
00:53:59,153 --> 00:54:01,467
<i>Now that I've had my revenge...</i>

725
00:54:03,115 --> 00:54:04,794
<i>Goodbye.</i>

726
00:54:04,794 --> 00:54:07,743
This tragic fate of having to kill...

727
00:54:08,508 --> 00:54:11,438
the person she loves with her own hands.

728
00:54:17,708 --> 00:54:19,310
Is that it?

729
00:54:20,094 --> 00:54:23,153
He couldn't fight for independence,
and he couldn't achieve love either?

730
00:54:23,153 --> 00:54:26,566
This would have a runtime of about 40 minutes.

731
00:54:26,566 --> 00:54:28,393
No wonder he can't make any money.

732
00:54:28,393 --> 00:54:31,735
Honey, stop going on
about money in front of them.

733
00:54:31,735 --> 00:54:34,781
Seriously, you're embarrassing me.

734
00:54:35,859 --> 00:54:37,946
[Mom, shall we have lunch together tomorrow?]
This is actually pretty good...

735
00:54:37,946 --> 00:54:39,726
Yum.

736
00:54:39,726 --> 00:54:41,699
- Just eat your chicken.
- Yeah.

737
00:54:41,699 --> 00:54:47,666
[Sorry, I'm going to be busy for a while...]

738
00:55:32,556 --> 00:55:36,014
If you want to see
that precious son of yours...

739
00:55:38,303 --> 00:55:41,197
you need to heal fast.

740
00:55:42,854 --> 00:55:44,605
Isn't it?

741
00:55:49,516 --> 00:55:52,227
Ah, I finally have some free time.

742
00:55:52,227 --> 00:55:54,828
Do you even know how I feel, honey?

743
00:55:54,828 --> 00:55:57,128
Do you even know what it's like
to be the breadwinner?

744
00:55:57,128 --> 00:55:58,503
- Jeez...
- Let's hurry home.

745
00:55:58,503 --> 00:56:00,934
- We'll go ahead first. See you again.
- Let's have one more drink before we go.

746
00:56:00,934 --> 00:56:02,239
- Take care on your way.
- Bye!

747
00:56:02,239 --> 00:56:04,555
- Bye!
- We'll go. Take care.

748
00:56:04,555 --> 00:56:06,716
Shame we have to go.

749
00:56:06,716 --> 00:56:09,569
- I'm not drunk.
- Alright, alright.

750
00:56:11,288 --> 00:56:13,085
Shall we go too?

751
00:56:13,085 --> 00:56:15,034
Yeah, sure.

752
00:56:18,449 --> 00:56:20,136
Are you going home?

753
00:56:20,136 --> 00:56:22,346
Yeah, so?

754
00:56:22,346 --> 00:56:24,319
- I'll take you home.
- Oh.

755
00:56:24,319 --> 00:56:27,496
It's just around the corner.
I'll get there myself.

756
00:56:31,176 --> 00:56:32,706
Mom.

757
00:57:02,629 --> 00:57:04,757
Mom!

758
00:57:04,757 --> 00:57:06,636
Mom!

759
00:57:08,501 --> 00:57:11,635
- Mom!
- I'm sorry, Soo Bin...

760
00:57:11,635 --> 00:57:15,364
- Mom is sorry.
- Look at me.

761
00:57:17,813 --> 00:57:22,394
I shouldn't let you see me like this...

762
00:57:23,547 --> 00:57:25,571
Don't say that.

763
00:57:25,571 --> 00:57:28,191
Someone else should be apologizing.

764
00:57:30,826 --> 00:57:32,988
Oh, Mom!

765
00:57:32,988 --> 00:57:35,114
No...

766
00:57:36,188 --> 00:57:38,115
No...

767
00:58:24,620 --> 00:58:28,537
You shouldn't have touched my mother.

768
00:58:34,471 --> 00:58:38,810
You're the one who hit her, not me.

769
00:58:38,810 --> 00:58:43,116
So why did you have to come back
and make such a mess of everything?

770
00:58:43,116 --> 00:58:45,978
I told you I don't like flaws.

771
00:58:48,603 --> 00:58:51,984
Stop talking nonsense. Before I kill you!

772
00:58:55,619 --> 00:58:58,092
You seem to have forgotten.

773
00:58:59,122 --> 00:59:03,126
That woman is my wife,

774
00:59:03,126 --> 00:59:05,752
not your mother!

775
00:59:08,858 --> 00:59:11,038
Never...

776
00:59:11,038 --> 00:59:15,894
come near my mother or me again.

777
00:59:15,894 --> 00:59:17,981
Don't come looking for us.

778
00:59:20,960 --> 00:59:23,252
Soo Bin!

779
00:59:23,252 --> 00:59:26,746
You have a talent for ruining people.

780
00:59:26,746 --> 00:59:29,915
And you'll run away again...

781
00:59:32,784 --> 00:59:35,136
like a coward.

782
00:59:35,136 --> 00:59:36,864
Well?

783
00:59:37,584 --> 00:59:39,621
We'll see.

784
00:59:39,621 --> 00:59:42,505
Because I will remain as your flaw forever.

785
00:59:42,505 --> 00:59:44,751
You think...

786
00:59:44,751 --> 00:59:47,544
you're only a flaw in my life?

787
00:59:54,887 --> 00:59:57,942
How foolish you are.

788
00:59:57,942 --> 01:00:00,658
You ran away just to save your own life.

789
01:00:00,658 --> 01:00:02,264
But she...

790
01:00:02,264 --> 01:00:06,021
almost died trying to catch you.

791
01:00:09,833 --> 01:00:12,629
<i>I heard Yi Jae woke up.</i>

792
01:00:12,629 --> 01:00:14,283
<i>Do you know why my daughter ended up like that?</i>

793
01:00:14,283 --> 01:00:16,091
<i>She was on her way to see your son...</i>

794
01:00:16,091 --> 01:00:19,115
<i>Where is he now? Bring him to me!</i>

795
01:00:19,115 --> 01:00:21,201
<i>I'll make him suffer the same way!</i>

796
01:00:21,201 --> 01:00:23,779
<i>I'll break his legs!</i>

797
01:00:23,779 --> 01:00:25,918
<i>Say something.</i>

798
01:00:25,918 --> 01:00:28,545
<i>Say something!</i>

799
01:00:28,545 --> 01:00:30,432
<i>What are you going to do about my daughter?</i>

800
01:00:30,432 --> 01:00:32,660
<i>What are you going to do? Let go of me!</i>

801
01:00:32,660 --> 01:00:34,048
<i>I won't let this go!</i>

802
01:00:34,048 --> 01:00:35,943
<i>I won't let either of you get away with this!</i>

803
01:00:35,943 --> 01:00:37,875
<i>- Director! Are you okay?
- I'm fine.</i>

804
01:00:37,875 --> 01:00:40,042
<i>- Yeah.
- Jeez...</i>

805
01:01:24,184 --> 01:01:28,230
<i>You think you're only a flaw in my life?</i>

806
01:01:28,230 --> 01:01:32,359
<i>Didn't you ruin that girl's life too?</i>

807
01:01:32,359 --> 01:01:35,946
<i>Woo Soo Bin, you're my one and only regret.</i>

808
01:01:35,946 --> 01:01:39,692
<i>Try going through that day yourself.
See how it feels.</i>

809
01:01:41,368 --> 01:01:43,857
<i>Then what if Moo Gyeom leaves her?</i>

810
01:01:46,665 --> 01:01:49,365
<i>Then of course, she can't say it.</i>

811
01:02:38,196 --> 01:02:40,462
<i>At last, I finished the script!</i>

812
01:02:40,462 --> 01:02:43,224
<i>Want to grab a drink to celebrate
finishing the first draft?</i>

813
01:02:43,224 --> 01:02:46,771
<i>I'm not staying here any longer.
I'm getting out.</i>

814
01:02:46,771 --> 01:02:47,851
<i>"Gyeongseong Love Song?"</i>

815
01:02:47,851 --> 01:02:50,896
<i>So this is the guy Ha Na was looking for?
Is this all because of him?</i>

816
01:02:50,896 --> 01:02:53,106
<i>- Hello?
- It's me, Manager Kang.</i>

817
01:02:53,106 --> 01:02:54,292
<i>Nice to meet you...</i>

818
01:02:54,292 --> 01:02:56,443
<i>Let's save the introductions
for after the hunt.</i>

819
01:02:56,443 --> 01:02:58,440
<i>Now? Why am I being left out?</i>

820
01:02:58,440 --> 01:02:59,614
<i>Let's just do it this way.</i>

821
01:02:59,614 --> 01:03:02,211
<i>Who does she think she is,
not knowing her place...</i>

822
01:03:02,211 --> 01:03:04,698
<i>- Ugh...
- Wait.</i>
